// Title: Regsvr32 DLL Execution With Uncommon Extension
// Sigma ID: 50919691-7302-437f-8e10-1fe088afa145
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-07-17 | Modified: 2023-05-24
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, stealth, T1574, execution
// Description: Detects a "regsvr32" execution where the DLL doesn't contain a common file extension.
// False positives:
//   - Other legitimate extensions currently not in the list either from third party or specific Windows components.
// References:
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/34221348-072d-4b70-93f3-aa71f6ebecad/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regsvr32_uncommon_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "REGSVR32.EXE") and (not(((ProcessCommandLine contains ".ax" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".cpl" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ocx") or isnull(ProcessCommandLine) or ProcessCommandLine =~ ""))) and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains ".ppl" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".bav")))
